    "result_text": "A hold (on a person or on a claim) no longer takes a claim out of what's claimed. All 4 acceptance tests in `bin/e2e` now pass.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Server:** I added `Person.countsClaimed` (`person/Person.java`). It follows the same rules as before, minus the hold check. `RollupService.snapshot` now adds up claimed amounts with it, so the ROLLUP `claimed=` and TOTALS `claimed-total=` audit fields include held claims. Due and overdue still use `countsLive`, so held claims stay out of those, as before.\n- **Front end:** `person-claimed` and `rollup-claimed-total` now come from their own list in `features/people/people.ts`, which keeps held claims. The due, overdue, settled/open and period figures still use the existing list that leaves them out.\n- I updated the comments that said a held claim \"counts in no live total\".\n\nDeferred claims, and open claims of a person whose retirement date has been reached, still don't count as claimed. The request only named holds, so I left those alone.\n\n**A second fix the test needed:** In scenario 2, a steward waives a claim whose due-by falls in a period that had already closed. The app refused that, but the test expects it to go through. The waive method's own description lists only three refusals (not a steward, wrong status, already waived), and a closed period isn't one of them. So `ClaimService.waive` no longer refuses because of a closed period. This change has nothing to do with holds; other claim actions still refuse in a closed period.\n\nI deleted the temporary debug spec I used to track this down.",
